{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971106-prison-chronicles","id":971106,"title":"Prison chronicles?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-16T20:03:26-07:00","id":971106,"title":"Prison chronicles?","content":"Has anyone ever tried a Blue Book game set in prison? It'd be a pretty interesting setting for ChroD. I've asked about it over on rpgnet, but I figured it's worth making a topic for here. Stone Ocean would be pretty great inspiration for one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T13:55:29-07:00","id":972107,"title":"","content":"I've never done it myself, but I've definitely considered it. While I'm not familiar with Stone Ocean, there are plenty of tv shows and movies from which to draw inspiration. <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0095904/\" target=\"_blank\">Prison</a> with Viggo Mortensen, the <a href=\"http://supernatural.wikia.com/wiki/Folsom_Prison_Blues\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Folsom Prison Blues&quot;</a> episode of <i>Supernatural</i>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyond_Re-Animator\" target=\"_blank\">Beyond Re-Animator</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alien_3\" target=\"_blank\">Alien<sup>3</sup></a>, and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mal%C3%A9fique\" target=\"_blank\">Mal\u00e9fique</a> are the ones I can think of that most directly relate to a CofD game, but depending on what sort of chronicle you want to run, movies like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Shawshank_Redemption\" target=\"_blank\">The Shawshank Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_Escape_(1994_film)\" target=\"_blank\">No Escape (1994)</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortress_(1992_film)\" target=\"_blank\">Fortress (1992)</a>, and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedlock_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">Wedlock</a> might be useful. There are a lot of horror movies set in asylums that could be easily reworked to be set in a prison instead.<br /> <br /> I've always thought that prison-based chronicles have a ton of potential. The characters could come from any walk of life and have pretty much any skills, with the only requirement being that at some point they made one very bad decision that got them locked up. (Though there's always the possibility that the guy who insists he's been wrongly accused might just be telling the truth.) Because the characters are watched constantly, it would be fairly easy to build up a sense of paranoia, as well as dramatic tension when they're having to do things on a tight schedule to avoid being caught by the guards. And the characters have to deal with the constant threat from guards and other prisoners while dealing with whatever supernatural threats they might face.<br /> <br /> As for that supernatural threat, the obvious direction would be that the prison is haunted or else being used as a feeding ground for vampires (since people die in prison all the time, and might be less likely to be missed). But it might be more interesting to go with something different, like the prison being some sort of God-Machine infrastructure, prisoners and guards forming some sort of cult performing human sacrifices, the prison being a hunting ground for a Beast, or some event in the prison's past having weakened the barrier between worlds allowing things from beyond to begin possessing prisoners and guards. Or some combination of several of those. And if I were to run a prison-based chronicle, I'd probably break with some of the common tropes of the genre, such as the warden being a corrupt tyrant. I might have him believe the characters deserve to be in prison, but otherwise be a decent person and even willing to overlook minor infractions and even aid them to a degree once he learns of the darkness lurking in his prison that the characters are investigating.<br /> <br /> If you do run a prison-based chronicle, I'd love to hear what you do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}